    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on stolen base efficiency and high-upside matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.29) headlines our starting nine as the primary engine for speed; his ability to exploit a slow delivery from the opposing starter, combined with a significant platoon advantage and a leadoff spot, makes him our most efficient play. **Yordan Alvarez** (72.69) trails closely behind, and while his platoon split against a lefty typically tempers expectations, his elite xwOBA of .475 remains impossible to fade. Meanwhile, **Colt Keith** (69.64) offers excellent value in the three-hole, buoyed by a highly favorable matchup against a starter with a 5.30 xERA, making him an essential component of our offensive stack.\n\nWe maintained a disciplined approach to our bench today, keeping **Casey Schmitt** (47.68) on the pine. While **Casey Schmitt** was the strongest consideration for a utility spot, his unfavorable park factors and lower raw projection relative to our current starters kept him out of the mix, as we prioritized the high-floor production of **Junior Caminero**. Risks remain on the periphery, particularly with **Dillon Dingler** (52.54), whose score is suppressed by a negative platoon shift against a right-handed arm. Owners should also monitor **Caleb Durbin**; despite a marginal score of 51.71, his situational value is propped up by his opportunistic base-stealing potential against a pitcher with a slow delivery. We are comfortable holding **Carson Benge** and **Jacob Gonzalez** on the bench today, as their projections fell well below our 40-point efficiency floor.",
